WEBVTT

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:01.490
Assalamu alaikum, everyone.

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:07.252
First, I want to thank the people under whose
leadership we worked on today's problem set:

00:00:07.252 --> 00:00:08.830
Dr. Mohammad Kaykobad sir,

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:14.900
Distinguished Professor at BRAC University and Chief
Judge; Shahriar Manzoor sir,

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.970
Associate Professor at Southeast University and
Judging Director;

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.140
and Mohammad Ashraful Islam,

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:25.460
Assistant Professor at Jahangirnagar University and
Judging Coordinator.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:29.880
For the ICPC 2025 preliminary and onsite contests,

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:35.610
problem review was done by me, Raihat Zaman Neloy,
Software Engineer at Google Ireland;

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:39.990
Muhammad Nafis Sadique, Senior Software Engineer at
Google Ireland;

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.670
and Pritom Kundu, Stony Brook University.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:50.530
Today's problem set had ten problems, and seven
distinct problems were solved.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:55.300
At least one problem was solved by 288 teams

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.030
out of 313. So, a big round of applause for all of
them.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:07.000
Problem A, Mission Hexa, was set by Irfanur Rahman
Rafio.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:10.170
The testers were Rumman Mahmud and Nafis Sadique.

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:13.330
Tariq Hasan Rizu was the alternate writer.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.530
Its categories were geometry, number theory and
combinatorics.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:22.497
Problem B, Boulevard of Broken Cars. The setter was
Pritom Kundu,

00:01:22.497 --> 00:01:25.460
and the tester was Irfanur Rahman Rafio,

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:27.830
and the alternate writer was Nafis Sadique.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.410
This problem's categories were data structures and
implementation.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.490
Problem C, Gas Reservoir.

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:37.140
The setter was Mohammad Ashraful Islam.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.700
The tester was Raihat Zaman Neloy.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:44.632
The alternate writers were Sharif Minhazul Islam and
Tariq Hasan Rizu.

00:01:44.632 --> 00:01:47.160
Categories: graph theory and ad hoc.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:53.940
Problem D, Save the Wonderland. The setter was me,
Raihat Zaman Neloy.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:57.650
The tester was Mukit Hasan, Software Engineer at
Oracle.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:03.220
The alternate writer was Pritom Kundu. Categories:
graph theory, greedy and binary search.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:08.760
Problem E, Love Marriage. The setter was Irfanur
Rahman Rafio.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:12.730
The tester was Rafid Bin Mostofa, and the alternate
writer was

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:17.170
Rafid Bin Mostofa. Categories: probability, range
query and greedy.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:20.630
Problem F, Morning Walk.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.970
The setter was Monirul Hasan sir.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:26.119
Tester: Irfanur Rahman Rafio. Alternate writer:

00:02:26.119 --> 00:02:29.910
Raihat Zaman Neloy. Categories: geometry and basic
physics.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.570
Problem G, Nonogram.

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:34.840
The setter was Pritom Kundu.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:39.000
The testers were Rafid Bin Mostofa and Irfanur
Rahman Rafio.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:42.230
Alternate writer: Nafis Sadique. Category: ad hoc.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.757
Some teams got Wrong Answer on this problem because
of capitalization.

00:02:45.757 --> 00:02:48.600
Otherwise, their first submission would have been
accepted.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:54.200
Problem H, Optimal Balancing Strategy. The setter
was

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:58.230
Tariq Hasan Rizu. The testers were Shahjalal Shohag

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.990
and Irfanur Rahman Rafio.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:04.262
The alternate writers were Muhiminul Islam Osim and
Rafid Bin Mostofa.

00:03:04.262 --> 00:03:07.030
Categories: sorting, number theory and greedy.

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:12.530
Problem I, Two Strings Attached. The setter was
Shahjalal Shohag.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:16.104
The testers were Rafid Bin Mostofa and Irfanur
Rahman Rafio,

00:03:16.104 --> 00:03:20.660
and the alternate writer was Nafis Sadique.
Category: data structures. And today's

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.130
C-Style String Length.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:25.400
The setter was our respected Shahriar Manzoor sir.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.528
The tester was Mahmodol Hassan Monna,

00:03:27.528 --> 00:03:31.160
and the alternate writer was Irfanur Rahman Rafio.
Category: ad hoc.

